{"kind":"report","text":"Completed preliminary static review of exact I1 runtime 4b91a2e4aaa5a73f8c0edd2040d2a61e8b978b99 from fully read 931be8c6159e53710987788612befd4a89dfa27c. All thirty changed paths are covered collectively; this completes only checker promise 9b328b62 under d644e535. Two P2 findings require disposition before complete I1 delivery.\n\nP2 — an admitted timed entry can be permanently unwritable at the byte limit. Change only lane timed[hold-end].attention[0].notify.reason to a nonempty ASCII string longer than the default 256 KiB entry limit. validate.ts 590–599 admits that reason and 726–731 adds no declaration-wide byte cap. Core canonicalizes/validates the declaration and retains it separately (133–141,166); ordinary founding and take-hold entries do not carry the timed reason (fixtures.ts 98–105). A normal accepted hold therefore reaches its deadline. effects.ts 139–142 then embeds the reason in its mandatory timed entry. turn.ts 229 calls seal; 268–278 throws Unfit(size) before any write, outside the waiting-input catch at 255–256. The transaction rolls back; the hold stays due, and this exceptional exit never reaches close/wake. Later drains meet the same unwritable entry. Ensure admitted timed drafts fit the entry bound, including notification/member expansion and fixed entry overhead, before admitting the duty. Merely catching/retrying this draft, dropping attention without an adopted rule, skipping expiry or raising an unexplained limit cannot discharge it. One compact supported producer witness suffices; no heavy sweep requested.\n\nP2 — reconcile already sealed receipt/mismatch precedence with dependency fetching. core.ts 197–202 fetches fact fields and returns dependency-unavailable before judgeAct's accepted-index check at judge.ts 86–90 and core 226/229. The existing answers.test.ts 46–66 fixture accepts a remark naming P and demonstrates local retention of P. Remove P from the resolver after acceptance, optionally restart, then submit the exact signed remark: the wrapper returns dependency-unavailable before reading its stored receipt. A different correctly signed intent under the consumed key can similarly hide the specified idempotency mismatch behind an unavailable fact. Adopted R1 section 4.2 lines 331/334 and recovery example 2014, plus runtime deltas 80/81, promise the same receipt/mismatch; R1 section 5.2 step 1 explicitly describes prefetch failure, and its waiting-input/drain rules also apply. This is a supported unresolved contract/source inconsistency, not a claim of unlimited availability during every outage. Define the precedence explicitly in the existing R1 follow-through and implement it consistently, for example immutable signature/address and accepted-key identity before dependencies for a new admission. Direct settle at core 241–250 already reads sealed evidence without ports and remains a separate recovery route. Keep every actual admission/authority/time check for new work; no duplicate drain finding.\n\nExisting reserve boundary 1f52493c is independently confirmed, not refiled: with scopeEntries 12/reserve 2, genesis plus three holds reaches head 9 (three ordinary entries per hold); core 217 still admits it. Alarm writes ends 10 and 11, then turn 208 refuses seq 12, leaving the third admitted duty live. Full per-duty capacity, retained-input and settlement accounting remains owned under that request and R1/R4/I1, including nested sends/checkpoints/outcomes/cleanup; temporary high-water numbers are not an assurance.\n\nSupplementary later repair, separately frozen: root and lifecycle auditor read the complete four-path 4b-to-3ed99af50e645d68c1885e5ef612b98a7e160588 diff through EOF. At 3ed, readFacts carries accumulated uses on no-item and judgeGenesis builds source plus deduplicated named uses before recording the refusal. The compact proof-before-zItem witness matches. That closes the exact early genesis retention case fb6f8e03 statically; it was still present at frozen 4b. Check order/source/refusal reason and no-entry ordinary-act behavior remain. No test execution or final source approval is claimed.\n\nArchitecture/security/simplicity conclusions within read scope: shared pure judges and fold, synchronous append/retention/fold transactions, exact stored definition/name binding, isolated test ports and default-refusing production authority/readers are coherent. No additional material SQLite fold/restart/index consistency defect found. A history response first materializes up to 201 full entries before trimming to the 1 MiB response budget (reads 103–107); that is bounded overfetch, potentially about 50.25 MiB of raw entry text at defaults, not an unbounded-read defect. Its full memory/CPU/storage costs remain for R4. The slot index is written but explicitly unused; bounded indexed page queries and update cost disclosure are not a measured workflow saving. Cloudflare development tooling (Wrangler/Miniflare/workerd/esbuild/sharp) belongs in S7 cold installation/setup accounting. No dependency implementation or installed-runtime compatibility certification.\n\nRead provenance: root personally read all complete new scope production bodies including testing (74,713-character numbered stream through EOF), full 62,972-character non-lock/non-production-source diff through EOF, all runtime delta 79–95, all new tests as written, and relevant adopted R1 4.2/5.2/5.3/12 plus validator/effect/fixture/judge/genesis contexts. Full prior derive reading transferred only through complete changes and independently verified unchanged Git identities for validator/effects/fixtures/judge. Independent auditors fully read storage/read/fold/retention/restart paths, turn/lifecycle/fixtures, RPC/authority/API contracts and installation/export/test boundaries. Installation auditor read every changed lock byte through EOF (unified-3 diff 57,017 bytes/1,752 LF; SHA-256 ede04ff87135f635de9ddbba77ebc5530f377611f430090db160427a31becb20). Root read only the first 13,000 characters of the combined 194,487-character diff and does not claim sole full combined-diff coverage; fresh source and separate complete diffs provide the collective coverage. The deterministic JSON thirty-path path/byte/LF/SHA-256 ledger has SHA-256 05b17233a6539ed09fb340a103d915e1ac004f55cd0fc31a572ffad0b7aa3d55. Key source hashes: core e867ac6eb29f71558fce506b0450a8f3dd427f082f3c6997c9994ab1e5816870; turn f8775dac83a0117c04c486cd85f60b9cb5c4c3c57893ea6f244404d78fd3b8b3; SQLite 52b2ab4313b91028d479a571056a2f0f90e5719fbd39da7fa730f4a6028ca264; reads aaac971ce0fa721bffd2eeefde38b797f94bd4e650cd20491ce52156791c49ba; runtime delta 29e8d7a4e5fdf07d305f3ec7fc46ec68948ebc7546ffbb94e946639aeb4c84a0. Later 3ed hashes: frame 23a06e0a12df61d8b6505ca6cead2aff4e57cab5ac88addff740f7e79ddabda5; genesis fd24332c0fd90ef59e5b32ddc3393ecfdc33aa0a4a32da0002b6b77d31028801; compose a9c60ee2a2cbf9b7eb99b6b591239897ec1ebc492208d32a36aeb2b8aacf5b05.\n\nProducer reports of 155 passing tests/typecheck/timings are attributed evidence, not checker-executed verification. All 95 delta choices remain proposed. Complete normal I1 review, composition/dispatcher/service bindings, authority/resolver/session integration, independent replay/client, removal and full application/cloud/browser/device/operator/unknown-effect duties remain owed. This is not R1 adoption, final I1 approval or measured 10x test economy. No project/test/build/install/typecheck/private diagnostic execution, source edit, merge, push, deployment or provider effect.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}